    "badgeClassName": "as-paper",
    "emoji": "📌",
    "category": "Binomial Distribution",
    "weightBadge": "S1",
    "topics": [
      "\\(X\\sim B(n,p)\\)",
      "\\(P(X=r)=\\binom{n}{r}p^r(1-p)^{n-r}\\)",
      "Mean \\(np\\)",
      "Variance \\(np(1-p)\\)"
    ]
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "topicGrid",
        "items": [
          {
            "title": "Conditions",
            "body": "Fixed number of trials \\(n\\); each trial has two outcomes (success/failure); constant probability \\(p\\); trials independent. Then \\(X\\sim B(n,p)\\)."
          },
          {
            "title": "Probability Formula",
            "body": "\\(P(X=r)=\\dbinom{n}{r}p^r(1-p)^{n-r}\\) for \\(r=0,1,2,\\ldots,n\\)."
          },
          {
            "title": "Mean and Variance",
            "body": "\\(E(X)=np\\), \\(\\text{Var}(X)=np(1-p)\\), \\(\\sigma=\\sqrt{np(1-p)}\\)."
          },
          {
            "title": "Cumulative Probabilities",
            "body": "Use tables or calculator: \\(P(X\\leq r)\\). Note: \\(P(X\\geq r)=1-P(X\\leq r-1)\\)."
          },
          {
            "title": "Normal Approximation",
            "body": "If \\(n\\) large and \\(p\\) close to 0.5: \\(X\\approx N(np,\\,np(1-p))\\) with continuity correction."
          },
          {
            "title": "Finding Unknown n or p",
            "body": "Set up equations using given probabilities and solve. May require trial and error or logarithms for \\(n\\)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Binomial Distribution — Reference",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "If \\(X\\sim B(n,p)\\): \\(n\\) independent trials, each with probability \\(p\\) of success. \\(P(X=r)=\\dbinom{n}{r}p^r(1-p)^{n-r}\\). <strong>Mean:</strong> \\(E(X)=np\\). <strong>Variance:</strong> \\(\\text{Var}(X)=np(1-p)\\). Use the binomial distribution when: fixed \\(n\\), trials independent, constant \\(p\\), only 2 outcomes (success/failure).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "\\(P(X=r)\\)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\binom{n}{r}p^r(1-p)^{n-r}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Mean",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(np\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Variance",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(np(1-p)\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Conditions",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Fixed \\(n\\), independent, constant \\(p\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Exact probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\(X\\sim B(8,0.3)\\). Find (a) \\(P(X=3)\\), (b) \\(P(X\\leq1)\\).</p><p>(a) \\(P(X=3)=\\binom{8}{3}(0.3)^3(0.7)^5=56\\times0.027\\times0.16807\\approx0.2541\\).</p><p>(b) \\(P(X=0)=(0.7)^8\\approx0.0576\\); \\(P(X=1)=8(0.3)(0.7)^7\\approx0.1977\\). \\(P(X\\leq1)\\approx0.2553\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Finding n from mean",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>The mean of \\(X\\sim B(n,0.4)\\) is 6. Find \\(n\\) and the standard deviation.</p>\\[np=6\\Rightarrow n=15.\\quad\\sigma=\\sqrt{15\\times0.4\\times0.6}=\\sqrt{3.6}\\approx1.90.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "A fair coin is tossed 10 times. Find the probability of getting (a) exactly 6 heads, (b) fewer than 3 heads.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "(a) \\(\\binom{10}{6}(0.5)^{10}=210\\times\\tfrac{1}{1024}\\approx0.2051\\). (b) \\(P(X\\leq2)=P(0)+P(1)+P(2)=\\tfrac{1+10+45}{1024}=\\tfrac{56}{1024}\\approx0.0547\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
